      "Award programs sometimes zone LRD with SAT or AUS, making international redemptions possible at those airports' more competitive rates.",
      "American and United corporate contracts dominate LRD demand — booking outside peak business travel windows (Monday–Friday mornings) yields better pricing.",
    ],
    faqs: [
      {
        q: "What airlines fly from Laredo (LRD)?",
        a: "Laredo International Airport is served by American and United, with connections to Dallas/Fort Worth (DFW) and Houston (IAH). The trade-driven market creates consistent business travel demand on these routes.",
      },
      {
        q: "What are the cheapest flights from Laredo, Texas?",
        a: "LRD's most affordable routes connect to Dallas ($49–89 during flash sales) and Houston ($49–79). For broader domestic or international options, driving to San Antonio (2.5 hours) gives access to 12+ airlines. Award zone pricing occasionally places LRD in the same redemption tier as larger Texas airports.",
      },
      {
        q: "Is it worth driving from Laredo to San Antonio for flights?",
        a: "For major trips — especially international travel — yes. SAT's 12+ airlines and 55+ destinations offer far more options. For routine Dallas or Houston business travel, LRD's convenience is usually worth it over the 2.5-hour drive.",
      },
      {
        q: "When is the cheapest time to fly from Laredo (LRD)?",
        a: "September and January are typically the cheapest months from LRD. Business travel demand keeps weekday morning flights consistently priced — booking Friday afternoon or Sunday departures for leisure trips often yields better rates on the same routes.",
      },
    ],
  },
  ABI: {
    intro: "Abilene Regional Airport (ABI) serves West-Central Texas with American Eagle connections to DFW. The small market serves Abilene's university and military community (Dyess Air Force Base), with demand patterns driven by Abilene Christian University and Hardin-Simmons University's calendars. Award zone pricing often places ABI in the same tier as DFW for international redemptions.",
    stats: [
      { label: "Annual passengers", value: "300K+" },
      { label: "Primary connection", value: "DFW via AA Eagle" },
      { label: "Drive time to DFW", value: "3 hrs" },
      { label: "Drive time to AUS", value: "3 hrs" },
    ],
    routes: [
      { destination: "Dallas / DFW", typical: "$80–$180", errorFare: "$39–$79" },
      { destination: "International (via DFW)", typical: "Hub connection", errorFare: "DFW zone" },
      { destination: "Austin (AUS)", typical: "3 hr drive", errorFare: "75+ destinations" },
      { destination: "Dallas (DFW)", typical: "3 hr drive", errorFare: "260+ destinations" },
    ],
    tips: [
      "ABI's single hub connection means the best strategy for major trips is often driving to DFW or AUS — or using ABI-to-DFW as a first leg to international travel.",
      "Award programs frequently zone ABI with DFW — the same miles from Abilene can reach the same international destinations as from Dallas.",
      "University calendars (ACU, HSU) create predictable demand spikes during graduation (May), move-in (August), and Thanksgiving — book outside these windows.",
      "Dyess AFB military personnel should check Space-A availability alongside commercial deal alerts from ABI.",
    ],
    faqs: [
      {
        q: "What airlines fly from Abilene (ABI)?",
        a: "Abilene Regional Airport is served by American Eagle (American Airlines' regional carrier), with connections to Dallas/Fort Worth (DFW). The single hub connection provides access to American's full domestic and international network via DFW.",
      },
      {
        q: "What are the cheapest flights from Abilene, Texas?",
        a: "ABI's routes connect to DFW ($39–79 during flash sales). For international travel or destinations not directly served via DFW, driving to Austin or Dallas (both ~3 hours) offers significantly more options. Award programs often zone ABI identically to DFW for international redemptions.",
      },
      {
        q: "Is it worth flying from Abilene or driving to Dallas?",
        a: "For convenience on frequent business travel to Dallas, ABI is practical. For any other destination, driving 3 hours to DFW or AUS gives you 260+ and 75+ destinations respectively vs. ABI's single hub connection. For major leisure trips, the drive is almost always worthwhile.",
      },
      {
        q: "When is the cheapest time to fly from Abilene (ABI)?",
        a: "January, February, and September are cheapest from ABI. Avoid graduation weekend (May), university move-in (August), and Thanksgiving — all create demand spikes on the limited DFW schedule. Given few daily departures, booking 4–6 weeks in advance secures better availability.",
      },
    ],
  },
};

const airportContent = AIRPORT_CONTENT[airportData.code] ?? null;

const airportMeta = AIRPORT_META[airportData.code] ?? {
  title: `${airportData.code} Cheap Flights: Live Deals`,
  description: `Find live and archived flight deals from ${airportData.city}, including route-specific fare drops and Texas airport alerts from ${airportData.code}.`,
};
const title = `${airportMeta.title} | Texas Cheap Flights`;
const description = airportMeta.description;

// JSON-LD for the airport page
const jsonLd = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@graph": [
    {
      "@type": "WebPage",
      "@id": `${Astro.url.href}#webpage`,
      "url": Astro.url.href,
      "name": title,
      "description": description,
      "breadcrumb": {
        "@id": `${Astro.url.href}#breadcrumb`
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
      "@id": `${Astro.url.href}#breadcrumb`,
      "itemListElement": [
        {
          "@type": "ListItem",
          "position": 1,
          "name": "Texas Cheap Flights",
          "item": "https://texascheapflights.com/"
        },
        {
          "@type": "ListItem",
          "position": 2,
          "name": `Deals from ${airportData.city}`,
          "item": Astro.url.href
        }
      ]
    },
    ...(airportContent?.faqs?.length ? [{
      "@type": "FAQPage",
      "mainEntity": airportContent.faqs.map(faq => ({
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": faq.q,
        "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": faq.a }
      }))
    }] : [])
  ]
};
---

<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
  <title>{title}</title>
  <meta name="description" content={description} />
  <link rel="canonical" href={`https://texascheapflights.com/deals/from/${airport?.toLowerCase()}`} />
  
  <meta property="og:title" content={title} />
  <meta property="og:description" content={description} />
  <meta property="og:type" content="website" />
  <meta property="og:image" content="https://texascheapflights.com/og-image.png" />
  
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(jsonLd)} />
  
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin />
  <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Satoshi:wght@400;500;700;900&family=Outfit:wght@400;500;700&display=swap" rel="stylesheet" />
</head>
<body class="bg-tcf-navy-deep text-white min-h-screen">

  <GlobalNav activePage="past-deals" />

  <main class="pt-32 pb-24 px-6">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
      
      <header class="mb-16">
        <span class="text-tcf-gold font-bold text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.3em] mb-4 inline-block">Regional Airport Scout</span>
        <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-6xl font-black mb-6 leading-tight">
          Cheap Flights from <br/><span class="text-gold italic">{airportData.city} ({airportData.code})</span>
        </h1>
        <p class="text-lg text-slate-400 max-w-2xl font-body leading-relaxed">
          We monitor every major airline and award program departing from {airportData.city}. No more generic alerts for DFW when you're flying out of {airportData.code}.
        </p>
      </header>

      {dealList.length > 0 ? (
        <div class="space-y-6">
          <h2 class="text-sm font-black text-white uppercase tracking-widest mb-8">Recent Alerts from {airportData.code}</h2>
          <div class="grid gap-4">
            {dealList.map((deal) => (
              <a href={`/deal/${deal.id}`} class="block liquid-glass p-6 rounded-2xl border border-white/5 hover:border-tcf-gold/30 transition-all duration-300 group no-underline text-inherit">
                <div class="flex justify-between items-center">
                  <div>
                    <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-2">
                        <span class={`text-[10px] font-black uppercase tracking-widest px-2 py-0.5 rounded-full border ${deal.score >= 8 ? 'text-tcf-gold border-tcf-gold/30 bg-tcf-gold/5' : 'text-slate-500 border-white/10'}`}>
                            Score: {deal.score}/10
                        </span>
                        <span class="text-[10px] text-slate-500">{new Date(deal.sent_at).toLocaleDateString()}</span>
                    </div>
                    <div class="text-xl font-black text-white group-hover:text-tcf-gold transition-colors">{deal.origin} → {deal.destination}</div>
                    <div class="text-xs text-slate-500 mt-1">{deal.airline} · {deal.travel_dates}</div>
                  </div>
                  <div class="text-right">
                    <div class="text-2xl font-black text-white">{deal.price ? `$${deal.price}` : 'Points'}</div>
                    <div class="text-[10px] text-slate-500 uppercase tracking-widest mt-1">Roundtrip</div>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </a>
            ))}
          </div>
        </div>
      ) : (
        <div class="space-y-6">
          <!-- Scout Status Card -->
          <div class="p-8 rounded-[2rem] liquid-glass border border-tcf-gold/20">
            <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-6">
              <span class="relative flex h-3 w-3">
                <span class="animate-ping absolute inline-flex h-full w-full rounded-full bg-tcf-gold opacity-75"></span>
                <span class="relative inline-flex rounded-full h-3 w-3 bg-tcf-gold"></span>
              </span>
              <span class="text-xs font-black text-tcf-gold uppercase tracking-[0.2em]">AI Scout Active — {airportData.code}</span>
            </div>
            <h3 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-3">No archived deals yet — Scout is watching.</h3>
            <p class="text-slate-400 leading-relaxed font-body max-w-xl">
              Our AI hasn't flagged a sendable deal from {airportData.city} yet, but the radar is live. Error fares and award arbitrage windows from {airportData.code} tend to be brief — most close within 2–4 hours. Subscribers get the alert the moment one surfaces.
            </p>
          </div>

          <!-- What We Watch For -->
          <div class="grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-4">
            <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl bg-white/5 border border-white/5">
              <p class="text-xs font-black text-tcf-gold uppercase tracking-widest mb-3">Error Fares</p>
              <p class="text-sm text-slate-400 leading-relaxed font-body">Airline pricing glitches that can slip through for hours before the carrier pulls them. Legal to book, often honored, but never guaranteed.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl bg-white/5 border border-white/5">
              <p class="text-xs font-black text-tcf-aviation-blue uppercase tracking-widest mb-3">Zone Awards</p>
              <p class="text-sm text-slate-400 leading-relaxed font-body">Award programs price by zone, not distance. {airportData.code} often costs the same points as DFW or IAH to the same destination.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl bg-white/5 border border-white/5">
              <p class="text-xs font-black uppercase tracking-widest mb-3" style="color: var(--tcf-success)">Sweet Spots</p>
              <p class="text-sm text-slate-400 leading-relaxed font-body">Partner award pricing that's mispriced relative to cash. Rare but high-value — often 70–80% below retail.</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- CTA -->
          <div class="p-8 rounded-[2rem] bg-tcf-gold/5 border border-tcf-gold/20 flex flex-col md:flex-row items-center justify-between gap-6">
            <div>
              <p class="font-black text-white text-lg mb-1">Get the first alert when a deal drops from {airportData.city}.</p>
              <p class="text-sm text-slate-400 font-body">No spam. One alert per deal. Unsubscribe in one click.</p>
            </div>
            <a href="/#waitlist" class="btn-primary whitespace-nowrap no-underline" style="background: var(--tcf-gold); color: #050a14; font-weight: 900; padding: 0.75rem 2rem; border-radius: 9999px; font-size: 0.875rem; letter-spacing: 0.1em; text-transform: uppercase;">
              Alert Me for {airportData.code}
            </a>
          </div>
        </div>
      )}

      <!-- Rich Airport Content Section -->
      <section class="mt-24 pt-24 border-t border-white/5">
        {airportContent ? (
          <div class="space-y-20">

            <!-- Intro + Stats -->
            <div>
              <p class="text-slate-300 text-lg leading-relaxed max-w-3xl font-body mb-10">{airportContent.intro}</p>
              <div class="grid grid-cols-2 md:grid-cols-4 gap-4">
                {airportContent.stats.map(stat => (
                  <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/5 text-center">
                    <div class="text-2xl font-black text-white">{stat.value}</div>
                    <div class="text-xs text-slate-500 mt-1 uppercase tracking-wider">{stat.label}</div>
                  </div>
                ))}
              </div>
            </div>

            <!-- Historical Deal Ranges -->
            <div>
              <h2 class="text-xl font-black text-white mb-2">Typical vs. Error Fare Prices from {airportData.city}</h2>
              <p class="text-sm text-slate-500 mb-6 font-body">Historical ranges based on observed deals. Error fares close within 2–6 hours — subscribe to get notified instantly.</p>
              <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-2xl border border-white/10">
                <table class="w-full text-sm min-w-[500px]">
                  <thead>
                    <tr class="bg-white/5 border-b border-white/10">
                      <th class="text-left px-4 py-3 text-xs text-slate-500 font-bold uppercase tracking-wider">Destination</th>
                      <th class="text-left px-4 py-3 text-xs text-slate-500 font-bold uppercase tracking-wider">Typical Price</th>
                      <th class="text-left px-4 py-3 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider" style="color: var(--tcf-gold);">Error Fare Range</th>
                    </tr>
                  </thead>
                  <tbody>
                    {airportContent.routes.map((route, i) => (
                      <tr class={`border-b border-white/5 ${i % 2 === 0 ? '' : 'bg-white/[0.02]'}`}>
                        <td class="px-4 py-3 font-bold text-white">{route.destination}</td>
                        <td class="px-4 py-3 text-slate-500 line-through text-sm">{route.typical}</td>
                        <td class="px-4 py-3 font-black" style="color: var(--tcf-gold);">{route.errorFare}</td>
                      </tr>
                    ))}
                  </tbody>
                </table>
              </div>
            </div>

            <!-- Pro Tips -->
            <div>
              <h2 class="text-xl font-black text-white mb-6">Pro Tips for Finding Cheap Flights from {airportData.city}</h2>
              <div class="space-y-3">
                {airportContent.tips.map((tip, i) => (
                  <div class="flex gap-4 p-4 rounded-xl bg-white/5 border border-white/5">
                    <span class="font-black text-sm mt-0.5 shrink-0" style="color: var(--tcf-gold);">{i + 1}.</span>
                    <p class="text-slate-300 text-sm leading-relaxed font-body">{tip}</p>
                  </div>
                ))}
              </div>
            </div>

            <!-- FAQ Section -->
            <div>
              <h2 class="text-xl font-black text-white mb-6">Frequently Asked Questions — Cheap Flights from {airportData.city}</h2>
              <div class="space-y-4">
                {airportContent.faqs.map(faq => (
                  <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl bg-white/5 border border-white/5">
                    <h3 class="font-black text-white mb-2 text-base">{faq.q}</h3>
                    <p class="text-slate-400 text-sm leading-relaxed font-body">{faq.a}</p>
                  </div>
                ))}
              </div>
            </div>

          </div>
        ) : (
          <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-12">
            <article class="prose prose-invert prose-sm max-w-none">
              <h3 class="text-white font-black text-lg mb-4">Why monitor {airportData.city}?</h3>
              <p class="text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
                Departing from {airportData.code} often means you're limited to regional connections or high-priced positioning flights. However, award programs often price {airportData.code} to international destinations the same as DFW or IAH. This creates arbitrage windows where you can fly from your backyard for the same price as a major airport.
              </p>
            </article>
            <article class="prose prose-invert prose-sm max-w-none">
              <h3 class="text-white font-black text-lg mb-4">Best Strategy for {airportData.code}</h3>
              <p class="text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
                Our AI Scout specifically looks for Zone-Based redemptions and error fares that propagate to regional TX feeders. For {airportData.city} travelers, we recommend keeping a stash of transferable points to lock in these windows before they vanish.
              </p>
            </article>
          </div>
        )}
      </section>
    </div>
  </main>

  <footer class="py-20 border-t border-white/5 text-center text-xs text-slate-600">
    <p>© 2026 Texas Cheap Flights · <a href="/past-deals" class="text-slate-500 hover:text-white transition-colors no-underline">Back to All Deals</a></p>
  </footer>

</body>
</html>
